Both algorithms agree on both cases. Here's a summary of the changes:

**`DfsCycleDetector.java`** (new file) — iterative DFS using an explicit `Deque<Frame>` to avoid recursion-stack overflow. Each `Frame` holds the current node and an `Iterator` over its neighbors. Nodes are colored `WHITE` → `GRAY` (on push) → `BLACK` (on pop). Encountering a `GRAY` neighbor is a back edge, confirming a cycle.

**`Algorithm.java`** — added `DFS` constant.

**`CycleDetectorFactory`** — added `case DFS: return new DfsCycleDetector()`.

